    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20665" root="سمد" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِسْمِيدٌ</span></b>  <i>What is called in Persian</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِمِدٌ</span> [app. a
mistranscription for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَمَذْ</span>, i. e. <i>white bread</i>]; an
arabicized word: [so says ISd; and he adds,] I
know not whether it be the same as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمِيدٌ</span> expl.
by Kr as signifying <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَعَامٌ</span>, or not. (M.)

